  "id": "COMPOUND:26744 - PROTEIN:4976",
  "verbalization": "Hex-4-enoic acid appears to be a common target for multiple compounds, all of which ultimately lead to HT-29, a human colorectal cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that Hex-4-enoic acid interacts with A2058, a protein that serves as a target for several structurally diverse molecules, including 5-[2-(2,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)ethyl]benzene-1,3-diol, (2S,3R,4R,5E,7S)-3,4,7-trihydroxy-2-propyl-2,3,4,7,8,9-hexahydrooxecin-10-one, and (15aS)-13,14,15,15a-Tetrahydro-3-methoxy-5H,11H-pyrrolo(2,1-c)quinazolino(3,2-a)(1,4)benzodiazepine-5,11-dione. These compounds, despite their varied chemical structures, all share a common mechanism of action: they target A2058 and ultimately influence HT-29 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Hex-4-enoic acid in modulating HT-29 cell behavior through the regulation of A2058, suggesting a broader pharmacological impact on cancer cell proliferation. The consistent presence of A2058 as a target across these pathways underscores the importance of this protein in the observed effects, and the shared outcome of HT-29 cell inhibition reinforces the significance of this interaction.",
